{
  "title": "Stage 2: A generic store",
  "summary": "Write Repository<T> and Result<T> once, constrain them to entities, and swap stores without touching callers.",
  "minutes": 25,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Somewhere to keep the orders",
      "body": [
        "Accepted orders have to be stored, and the store must refuse a second order with the same id. You could write an `OrderStore` class. But next month you will want a store for customers, then one for invoices, each with the same `Add`, `Find` and `All`. That is the job of a **generic** class, written once with a type parameter:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "interface IEntity { int Id { get; } }",
        "",
        "interface IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    Result<T> Add(T item);",
        "    T? Find(int id);",
        "    IReadOnlyList<T> All();",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "The constraint `where T : IEntity` is what makes it useful: inside the repository the compiler knows every `T` has an `Id`, so `item.Id` compiles. Without it, `T` could be `int` or `string`, and `item.Id` would be an error.",
        "",
        "`Add` can fail (duplicate id), and failing is normal, not exceptional. So it returns a small generic **result** instead of throwing:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "record Result<T>(bool IsOk, T? Value, string Error)",
        "{",
        "    public static Result<T> Ok(T value) => new(true, value, \"\");",
        "    public static Result<T> Fail(string error) => new(false, default, error);",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "Validation returns a `Result<Order>` too, so the loop reads as one chain: validate, then store, then report.",
        "",
        "Finally, the program holds the store as `IRepository<Order>`, the **interface**. That is what lets you swap in a completely different store later by changing one line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "`class ListRepository<T> : IRepository<T>` has **no** `where T : IEntity` constraint. What happens at `if (Find(item.Id) is not null)`?",
      "options": [
        "Compile error: `T` does not contain a definition for `Id`",
        "It compiles, and throws at run time if `T` has no `Id`",
        "It compiles, and `item.Id` is always 0",
        "It compiles, because `IRepository<T>` already has the constraint"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "The compiler only lets you use members it can prove every `T` has. An unconstrained `T` could be anything, so it only has `object`'s members. A class must repeat the constraint of the interface it implements."
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Match each piece of the generic code to what it does.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "`where T : IEntity`",
          "Promises every `T` has an `Id`"
        ],
        [
          "`Result<T>.Fail(\"duplicate id 1\")`",
          "Reports a failure without throwing"
        ],
        [
          "`IRepository<Order> orders = ...`",
          "Callers depend on the interface, not a class"
        ],
        [
          "`T? Find(int id)`",
          "Returns `default` when nothing matches"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var store = new Store<Book>();",
        "Console.WriteLine(store.Add(new Book(1, \"Dune\")).IsOk);",
        "Console.WriteLine(store.Add(new Book(1, \"Emma\")).Error);",
        "Console.WriteLine(store.Find(1)?.Title);",
        "",
        "interface IEntity { int Id { get; } }",
        "",
        "record Book(int Id, string Title) : IEntity;",
        "",
        "record Result<T>(bool IsOk, string Error);",
        "",
        "class Store<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    private readonly Dictionary<int, T> _items = new();",
        "",
        "    public Result<T> Add(T item) =>",
        "        _items.TryAdd(item.Id, item)",
        "            ? new Result<T>(true, \"\")",
        "            : new Result<T>(false, $\"duplicate id {item.Id}\");",
        "",
        "    public T? Find(int id) => _items.TryGetValue(id, out var item) ? item : default;",
        "}"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "True",
        "duplicate id 1",
        "Dune"
      ],
      "explain": "`record Book(int Id, ...)` gets a public `Id` property, which satisfies `IEntity`. `TryAdd` refuses the second id 1, so the first book stays."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "A generic repository",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Store the accepted orders.",
        "",
        "1. Add `interface IEntity { int Id { get; } }` and make `Order` implement it: `record Order(...) : IEntity;` (the record's `Id` property already satisfies it).",
        "2. Add the `Result<T>` record from the card, with `Ok` and `Fail`.",
        "3. Add `interface IRepository<T> where T : IEntity` with `Result<T> Add(T item)`, `T? Find(int id)` and `IReadOnlyList<T> All()`.",
        "4. Write `class ListRepository<T> : IRepository<T> where T : IEntity`, backed by a `List<T>`. `Add` fails with `duplicate id N` if an item with that id is already stored. `All` returns items in the order they were added.",
        "5. Move the rule checks into `Result<Order> Validate(Order order)`: `Ok(order)` when no rule objects, otherwise `Fail` with the reasons joined by `; `.",
        "6. In the loop: validate; if that worked, `orders.Add(order)`; print `accepted` or `rejected: ERROR` from whichever result came last. Declare the store as `IRepository<Order> orders = new ListRepository<Order>();`.",
        "",
        "After the summary line, print `Stored: ` and the stored ids as `#N` joined by `, `, or `Stored: none`.",
        "For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "7,bob,gadget,1",
        "1,alice,widget,3",
        "1,carol,widget,2",
        "3,dave,widget,2",
        "3,mallory,widget,1",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "#7 bob Gadget x1 accepted",
        "#1 alice Widget x3 accepted",
        "#1 carol Widget x2 rejected: duplicate id 1",
        "#3 dave Widget x2 accepted",
        "#3 mallory Widget x1 rejected: customer mallory is blocked",
        "Accepted: 3, Rejected: 2, Unreadable: 0",
        "Stored: #7, #1, #3",
        "```",
        "",
        "Rules run first, so `#3 mallory` is rejected for being blocked, not as a duplicate."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "var rules = new List<IOrderRule>",
        "{",
        "    new MinQuantityRule(),",
        "    new MaxQuantityRule(10),",
        "    new DiscontinuedRule(Product.Gizmo),",
        "    new BlockedCustomerRule(\"mallory\"),",
        "};",
        "",
        "int accepted = 0, rejected = 0, unreadable = 0;",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "",
        "    var order = ParseOrder(line);",
        "    if (order is null)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"line {lineNumber}: cannot read '{line}'\");",
        "        unreadable++;",
        "        continue;",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    var reasons = rules.Select(rule => rule.Check(order)).OfType<string>().ToList();",
        "    if (reasons.Count == 0)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{Describe(order)} accepted\");",
        "        accepted++;",
        "    }",
        "    else",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{Describe(order)} rejected: {string.Join(\"; \", reasons)}\");",
        "        rejected++;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Accepted: {accepted}, Rejected: {rejected}, Unreadable: {unreadable}\");",
        "",
        "Order? ParseOrder(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[0], out var id)) return null;",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Product>(parts[2], ignoreCase: true, out var product) || !Enum.IsDefined(product)) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[3], out var quantity)) return null;",
        "    return new Order(id, parts[1], product, quantity);",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Describe(Order order) => $\"#{order.Id} {order.Customer} {order.Product} x{order.Quantity}\";",
        "",
        "enum Product { Widget, Gadget, Gizmo }",
        "",
        "record Order(int Id, string Customer, Product Product, int Quantity);",
        "",
        "interface IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    string? Check(Order order);",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MinQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity < 1 ? \"quantity must be at least 1\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MaxQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly int _max;",
        "",
        "    public MaxQuantityRule(int max) => _max = max;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity > _max ? $\"quantity over {_max}\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class DiscontinuedRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly Product _product;",
        "",
        "    public DiscontinuedRule(Product product) => _product = product;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Product == _product ? $\"{_product} is discontinued\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class BlockedCustomerRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly string _customer;",
        "",
        "    public BlockedCustomerRule(string customer) => _customer = customer;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Customer == _customer ? $\"customer {_customer} is blocked\" : null;",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "var rules = new List<IOrderRule>",
        "{",
        "    new MinQuantityRule(),",
        "    new MaxQuantityRule(10),",
        "    new DiscontinuedRule(Product.Gizmo),",
        "    new BlockedCustomerRule(\"mallory\"),",
        "};",
        "",
        "IRepository<Order> orders = new ListRepository<Order>();",
        "",
        "int accepted = 0, rejected = 0, unreadable = 0;",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "",
        "    var order = ParseOrder(line);",
        "    if (order is null)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"line {lineNumber}: cannot read '{line}'\");",
        "        unreadable++;",
        "        continue;",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    var result = Validate(order);",
        "    if (result.IsOk)",
        "        result = orders.Add(order);",
        "",
        "    if (result.IsOk)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{Describe(order)} accepted\");",
        "        accepted++;",
        "    }",
        "    else",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{Describe(order)} rejected: {result.Error}\");",
        "        rejected++;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Accepted: {accepted}, Rejected: {rejected}, Unreadable: {unreadable}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine(StoredLine(orders.All()));",
        "",
        "Result<Order> Validate(Order order)",
        "{",
        "    var reasons = rules.Select(rule => rule.Check(order)).OfType<string>().ToList();",
        "    return reasons.Count == 0",
        "        ? Result<Order>.Ok(order)",
        "        : Result<Order>.Fail(string.Join(\"; \", reasons));",
        "}",
        "",
        "string StoredLine(IReadOnlyList<Order> stored) =>",
        "    stored.Count == 0",
        "        ? \"Stored: none\"",
        "        : \"Stored: \" + string.Join(\", \", stored.Select(o => $\"#{o.Id}\"));",
        "",
        "Order? ParseOrder(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[0], out var id)) return null;",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Product>(parts[2], ignoreCase: true, out var product) || !Enum.IsDefined(product)) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[3], out var quantity)) return null;",
        "    return new Order(id, parts[1], product, quantity);",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Describe(Order order) => $\"#{order.Id} {order.Customer} {order.Product} x{order.Quantity}\";",
        "",
        "enum Product { Widget, Gadget, Gizmo }",
        "",
        "record Order(int Id, string Customer, Product Product, int Quantity) : IEntity;",
        "",
        "interface IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    string? Check(Order order);",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MinQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity < 1 ? \"quantity must be at least 1\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MaxQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly int _max;",
        "",
        "    public MaxQuantityRule(int max) => _max = max;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity > _max ? $\"quantity over {_max}\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class DiscontinuedRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly Product _product;",
        "",
        "    public DiscontinuedRule(Product product) => _product = product;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Product == _product ? $\"{_product} is discontinued\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class BlockedCustomerRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly string _customer;",
        "",
        "    public BlockedCustomerRule(string customer) => _customer = customer;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Customer == _customer ? $\"customer {_customer} is blocked\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "interface IEntity",
        "{",
        "    int Id { get; }",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Result<T>(bool IsOk, T? Value, string Error)",
        "{",
        "    public static Result<T> Ok(T value) => new(true, value, \"\");",
        "    public static Result<T> Fail(string error) => new(false, default, error);",
        "}",
        "",
        "interface IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    Result<T> Add(T item);",
        "    T? Find(int id);",
        "    IReadOnlyList<T> All();",
        "}",
        "",
        "class ListRepository<T> : IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    private readonly List<T> _items = new();",
        "",
        "    public Result<T> Add(T item)",
        "    {",
        "        if (Find(item.Id) is not null)",
        "            return Result<T>.Fail($\"duplicate id {item.Id}\");",
        "        _items.Add(item);",
        "        return Result<T>.Ok(item);",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public T? Find(int id) => _items.FirstOrDefault(i => i.Id == id);",
        "",
        "    public IReadOnlyList<T> All() => _items;",
        "}"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "duplicates are rejected, insertion order kept",
          "stdin": [
            "7,bob,gadget,1",
            "1,alice,widget,3",
            "1,carol,widget,2",
            "3,dave,widget,2",
            "3,mallory,widget,1"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "#7 bob Gadget x1 accepted",
            "#1 alice Widget x3 accepted",
            "#1 carol Widget x2 rejected: duplicate id 1",
            "#3 dave Widget x2 accepted",
            "#3 mallory Widget x1 rejected: customer mallory is blocked",
            "Accepted: 3, Rejected: 2, Unreadable: 0",
            "Stored: #7, #1, #3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "stage 1 input still works",
          "stdin": [
            "1,alice,widget,3",
            "2,bob,gadget,0",
            "3,carol,gizmo,2",
            "oops",
            "4,dave,Gadget,1"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "#1 alice Widget x3 accepted",
            "#2 bob Gadget x0 rejected: quantity must be at least 1",
            "#3 carol Gizmo x2 rejected: Gizmo is discontinued",
            "line 4: cannot read 'oops'",
            "#4 dave Gadget x1 accepted",
            "Accepted: 2, Rejected: 2, Unreadable: 1",
            "Stored: #1, #4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "no input",
          "stdin": "",
          "expect": [
            "Accepted: 0, Rejected: 0, Unreadable: 0",
            "Stored: none"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "interface\\s+IRepository<T>\\s+where\\s+T\\s*:\\s*IEntity",
          "message": "IRepository<T> is constrained to IEntity"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "class\\s+ListRepository<T>\\s*:\\s*IRepository<T>\\s+where\\s+T\\s*:\\s*IEntity",
          "message": "ListRepository<T> implements IRepository<T>"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "record\\s+Result<T>",
          "message": "Declares a generic Result<T>"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "IRepository<Order>\\s+orders",
          "message": "The program holds the store as IRepository<Order>"
        }
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\b(?:catch|try)\\s*[\\{\\(]",
          "message": "Reports duplicates without exceptions"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`Add`: `if (Find(item.Id) is not null) return Result<T>.Fail($\"duplicate id {item.Id}\"); _items.Add(item); return Result<T>.Ok(item);`",
        "`Find` can be `_items.FirstOrDefault(i => i.Id == id);`",
        "The loop: `var result = Validate(order); if (result.IsOk) result = orders.Add(order);` then print based on `result.IsOk` and `result.Error`."
      ]
    },
    {
